  "name": "Four Bar Riser",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "A four-bar riser into the drop: pitch and brightness climb across the phrase while a hiss builds in and the reverb tail swells. Hold one note for four bars, C3 works best, mono; the climb locks to the host tempo and restarts on every note. Macros: Rise Width brings in chorus; Noise Level raises the hiss; Pitch Rise lifts how far it climbs; Reverb Tail swells the wash.",
